{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Moshe cried out to YHWH concerning the matter of the frogs.</b> You will not find in the other plagues that he goes back to mention the plague along with the prayer, but it says simply 'and he entreated YHWH' and 'and he spread out his hands to YHWH.'" "<b>But</b> it is possible to explain that here it was necessary to say 'concerning the matter of the frogs,' because the Holy One, blessed be He, used for Moshe the language of ascent — that is, He said, ״ושרץ היאור צפרדעים ועלו ובאו בביתך״, and likewise Moshe said to Aharon, ״והעל את הצפרדעים״, and so it is written above in the account of the deed, ״ותעל הצפרדע״. And lest you understand from this language of ascent, which is mentioned every time, that the frogs came by way of nature and chance through artifice and wisdom like the wisdom of the sorcerers, and that this was not from YHWH — therefore it says, ״על דבר הצפרדעים אשר שם לפרעה״, to make clear that the Master of all, blessed be He, set this plague upon Pharaoh, and not the power of nature."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:59.798797068Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}